CODEGEN.md §2.4 (DECISIONS 451): a single-file load of a path an emit will write, which does not exist yet, keeps E7004 "cannot read" on every run (its build fails, so the file is never written); only a load.dir pattern is E8026 before the output exists.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  roots {
    data: "a/data"
  }
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// R.
record R {
  /// The value.
  v: Int
}

/// One.
let one: [R] = load("data/y.json")
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// Note.
@text("y.json")
export fn note() -> String { return "y\n" }

emit text { out: "@data" }
-- a/data/x.json --
{"v": 1}
-- check-only --
-- findings.txt --
error[E7004]  a/a.canon:11:16
  cannot read a/data/y.json: no such file or directory

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
